A||||12||Dan010||auto trans service||||1||
Z||000000||Dan010||12-17-2001||09:29 PM||||I have a 86gt auto with 90k.<BR>I have heard stories about auto trans that have not been serviced ( change fluid ect.)<BR>that this could cause new problems and even trans failure.<BR>Whats the expert opinions about this!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-17-2001||09:32 PM||||<B><FONT COLOR="red"><I>EXPERT OPINION</I></FONT></B> = change the transmission fluid and filter<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||NEPTUNE||12-18-2001||04:52 PM||||B&M Trick Shift works really well- crisper shifts. Try removing one of the rubber cooling hoses (next to the tranny), start the car and it will pump old fluid from the torque converter into a bucket. This will get more old, dirty fluid out than just draining it.Then lift the car, remove the pan, clean it and replace the filter. Fill 'er up and go!||||reg||10
Z||000003||theogre||12-18-2001||07:08 PM||||The method I use is in my cave... It's more detailed than Neptune's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>New filter and a fresh load of DexronIII will do wonders for it.<P>Main thing is make sure you don't over tighten the pan bolts and bend the pan. Check it on a flat surface to make sure it's rim is flat when you take it off. If bent carfully flatten it or find another pan. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan010||12-18-2001||07:20 PM||||On the wat home from work I stop by a <BR>Tranmission shop to find out when they <BR>might service my Fiero. They suggested "not"<BR>to change the fluid, and if there is no problem with the trans, dont do anything.<BR> Will check other places, or may do it myself. I believe you all more than the local<BR>shops.<BR>Any other thoughts?<BR>THanks for your opinions!!!!<BR>Dan||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dan010||12-18-2001||07:26 PM||||Forgot to mention, I did read Theogres info in his cave before starting to check into this. I have read almost everything in his cave.<BR>Also read everything I can from past treads on any subject I plan to look into.<BR>THANKS to all. Learning so much about the Fiero. Get a bit confussed about the different opinions on engine rebuild vs swap<BR>vs size. Guess money is the desiding factor!||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||12-18-2001||07:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dan010:<BR><B>On the wat home from work I stop by a <BR>Tranmission shop to find out when they <BR>might service my Fiero. They suggested "not"<BR>to change the fluid, and if there is no problem with the trans, dont do anything.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I would avoid this shop for future work!  <B>ALL</B> auto transmissions (no matter what type of car it is) should be serviced at the 100K mile mark......this is the bare minimum too.  When I drove an auto Fiero I serviced it every 40-50K miles.....better safe than sorry and it's cheap insurance.<P>I have also used B&M trick shift fluid and loved it......it's pricey (about $4/qt.), but really did firm up the shifts.<P>Either do it yourself or bring it to another shop that will do it for you.<BR> <BR>Good luck!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mark Matthews||12-18-2001||07:54 PM||||Gonna probably do this to mine as well, since it's right at 107K. How much fluid does it take, and can I put RedLine ATF in there?  Filter from Pontiac?<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dan010||12-18-2001||08:36 PM||||Which do you think is the better,<BR>Dexron III or<BR>B&M Trick Shift??<BR>For our auto trans. specially with 90k<BR>miles on it||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroRacer||12-18-2001||08:43 PM||||What if the tranny dipstick was already dry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  I'm thinking of redline after I'm sure there's been no permanent damage.  For now, walmart special.||||reg||1
Z||000010||GTDude||12-19-2001||10:02 AM||||When in doubt.....change it.....the fluid and the filter.  I prefer GM because of the superior gasket.  DexIII will work great in all applications except the most severe situations.  Such as a v-8.  B&M is a great product too......but expensive and not really necessary for most people.<P>phil pettus<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a_4.JPG"> <P>||||reg||3
Z||000011||Dan010||12-19-2001||01:14 PM||||Well, been calling a few shops around my area, get different prices. Any where from 30 to 50 dollars. Of course, with different opinions on to or not to change fluid.<BR>Some keep saying, if trans was ever over heated, changing trans fluid is not recomended, whould make the trans fail sooner.<P>I think I will give it a go this weekend.<BR>Thanks for all your advise!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Dan010||12-20-2001||01:08 PM||||I will be going to the trans shop this weekend. Is there any thing else I should make note of while at the shop, like any adjustments to bands ect.||||reg||1
